project introduction:
一个整合德国工作的网站，使用fastapi和jinja的template实现前后端。本项目包含两个硕士课程的presentation，现在实现第一部分，information retrieval,要实现的功能包含一个首页，展示当前的信息，然后一个搜索框，输入搜索内容，点击搜索，搜索结果按相关度排序展示。根据下面的要求实现搜索过程中涉及到的Information retrieval的知识并详细讲解，底层逻辑核心原理。检查当前代码进度，然后指导下一个阶段的计划，给我文字解释每一行代码的意思及整体的思路和逻辑，深入浅出，让我能够完全理解每一行代码。每次写完代码，检查5遍代码，确保满足要求、逻辑清晰、代码简洁、无冗余代码。
保持代码简洁，只包含必须的代码，实现最小可行性版本。

requirement:
As discussed in our previous sessions, I would like to remind you once again that your final project should demonstrate a working Information Retrieval system, not just theory. The focus is on how information is indexed, retrieved, ranked, and evaluated.
 
Your project must include all of the following components:
Dataset: clearly describe your dataset, source (e.g. text files, scraped data), size (number of documents), and type (news, reviews, articles)
Indexing and Representation: explain how documents are represented for example, tokenization, stop-word removal, stemming or lemmatization, term frequency, TI-IDF. 
Retrieval model: At least on IR model for example, Boolean Retrieval, Vector Space Model (cosine similarity), TF-IDF ranking.Bonus (BM25, Simple Query Expansion)
useBM25
Evaluation: you must include basic IR evaluation such as Accuarcy, Recall, Precision@K
Search interface: your system mush have a simple web interface, for example, search input field, list of ranked results, short snippet or highlighted terms
Hosting: your project should be deployed, not just run locally. A typical setup would be to use Python (Flask or FastAPI) for backend, IR logic, a CSS framework e.g. Bootstrap for frontend, and hosted online on e.g. PythonAnywhere. During the presentation, you should open the hosted URL, enter a query, explain why the results are ranked as shown. 
 
You have 15-20 minutes to present your project and the presentation format is slides + demo + code walkthrough